<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Setthathirath II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1730</span> · Also known as Sai Ong Hue</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/setthathirath">Setthathirath</a> II, also known as Sai Ong Hue, was a prince of Lan Xang who grew up in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. With Vietnamese backing he seized Vientiane around 1707 during a succession dispute, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> broke away under a rival line. He ruled the new Kingdom of Vientiane until about 1730, and the old kingdom of Lan Xang was never reunited.</p></div>
